 34NA c  2014Do05: a 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the
 34NA2c  superconducting ring cyclotron (SRC) at RIKEN. A 236-MeV/nucleon       
 34NA3c  {+36}Mg secondary beam was produced by the fragmentation of {+48}Ca on 
 34NA4c  a Be target and separated by the BigRIPS separator using the           
 34NA5c  B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction targets were 2.54-g/cm{+2}  
 34NA6c  thick carbon and 2.13-g/cm{+2} thick CH{-2} polyethylene. The secondary
 34NA7c  reaction products {+33}Na, {+34}Na, and {+35}Na were identified by the 
 34NA8c  magnetic spectrometer ZeroDegree using the B|r-|DE-ToF method. |g rays 
 34NA9c  in coincidence with {+34}Na were detected using the DALI2 array of 186 
 34NAAc  large NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, and
 34NABc  ({+34}Na)|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with shell-model            
 34NACc  calculations using the SPDF-M effective interaction.                   
